msgid "The build, and upload to the APM was flight tested by the author for the code release 3.1.3. The flight modes stabilize, altitude hold and loiter were all tested and behaved the same as upload of the same revision using Mission Planner.  However, be aware that building your own upload from the source can result in unexpected results. You must configure all the options defines and other code correctly. Be careful, have fun and enjoy Visual Studio with Visual Micro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:191
#: d035ef90b3884eea9c31f409c6abf57c
msgid "Hints and Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:193
#: 6768693ceca34046b11eff202a1b05e0
msgid "This procedure was tested to build and upload to the APM on the authors PC. There are other ways to configure Arduino, Atmel Studio, Visual Studio, and Visual Micro. Those methods are left to the reader. For instance, you can install the ArduPilot Arduino IDE in any location, not just in the Programs area. It is suggested to use this process first to verify everything works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:200
#: 94ef2507e8a1490dac46ed6a1bf0c6d5
msgid "**Ways to reduce the size of Copter so it will build:** In Visual Studio or Atmel Studio solution panel (where the source files are listed), open the file Copter/Header Files/APM_Config.h and un-comment some of the #Define XXX DISABLED lines to save some space. I.E. disable  MOUNT, OPTFLOW, CAMERA,CONFIG_SONAR and/or PARACHUTE as appropriate for your APM.  Each time you change a define you must do Build>>Clean Solution followed by Build>>Rebuild Solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:208
#: 99ce7c1868614553a3abafb8cdba250a
msgid "**Errors building from fresh source clone:**  The first time you set the application location (for instance after getting a fresh clone of the source) or change the IDE you are using, you may get build errors even though you have selected the correct Arduino board.  To get an error free build, just re-select the correct board. See Multiple installs of Arduino below for one reason this may occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:215
#: ef9c338b03ff43bca7a6a63e9d1f9a43
msgid "**Fast compile vs changing defines:**  Visual Micro has a default option for fast compiles. This is setup as the default. The IDE checks for changes to files and if there are no changes, does not recompile unchanged files.  This really great feature has a side effect when define statements are changed because they effect other files but do not specifically change the text (code) thus files effected by defines will not be recompiled causing a real mess.  There are two ways to avoid this issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:224
#: 6b52ce2703bb4c5183ff9359f95eb165
msgid "Each and every time you change a define or un-comment a define or comment a define do this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:227
#: f6ebd62398c044eab30b839fae6a88f0
msgid "Build>>Clean>>Solution (That will clean out the pre-compiled cache)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:228
#: 5f02e4a1e4624780b814816b1c3f2213
msgid "Build>>Rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:229
#: ae529244efa845f49b5398abb786d3d6
msgid "All following builds (assuming no changes to defines) can be the really fast version Build>>Build Solution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:232
#: e7425df9454b4909ab5d6b2e7e5dfad6
msgid "Or, if you like to wait a long time for each compile you can change the Visual Micro options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:235
#: c08312106d22468398764858a5ddada9
msgid "Tools>>Options.   Select Visual Micro. scroll down to Compiler Optimisation. Hey, in UK they spell it that way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:237
#: df51b38e975a4822a11327df251cfa5d
msgid "Set Core Modified and Library Modified to False"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:239
#: e56fe7167625491791612663e6c2f46a
msgid "Multiple installs of Arduino:  It is important to note that Arduino has only one location where the parameters are stored - in C:\\\\Users\\\\....\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\Arduino\\\\preferences.txt.  Any time you start any installation of Arduino - a standard version, the ArduPilot Arduino version or even changing settings in Visual Micro - that file may get changed.  So, it is very important to check all the settings in the IDE you are using each time you change the IDE - to avoid having the preferences set to that of the last IDE you used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:248
#: 9bf71a1079cc4151a0618875004b6fa9
msgid "**Referencing a standard Arduino in Visual Micro:** Normally, Visual Micro is setup to reference a standard installation of Arduino instead of the special ArduPilot Ardunio for the HAL versions of APM.  You can configure Visual Studio or Atmel Studio to reference a standard installation and it may build and upload the APM code but that upload will not work.  The build size is different and it does not connect to Mission Planner. It is strongly suggested you only reference the special ArduPilot Arduino installation when working with APM code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:257
#: c8d9875d7f13421292031d9872b5ca26
msgid "**Using Arduino statements and libraries:** This is better stated as not using standard Arduino statements.  The newer HAL versions of ArduPilot for the APM boards removed most, if not all, of the standard Arduino statements and libraries.  You can not just add an analogRead(sensorPin) statement for instance. So, do not be frustrated if you try to use the standard Arduino language reference to edit the APM code - it will mostly not work. There are equivalent calls and statements for the APM but you will have to search for examples in the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:268
#: a1e7883216bd430eb74c3a2b33c8de89
msgid "**Building Older Versions of ArduPilot:** If you are still working with version 2.9.1b or possibly older versions prior to HAL, you can take advantage of the Atmel Studio or Visual Studio and Visual Micro IDE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:273
#: c1c8d6724dad44bb97eae6d95de6a0a2
msgid "You just need to do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:275
#: beb0d3a319b4451fbd6dbb986cf3cb6d
msgid "Download the version of `ArduPilot Arduino that supports the 2.x.x revisions <https://code.google.com/archive/p/ardupilot-mega/downloads>`__. Don't confuse this with the current version. They have the same name but are different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:278
#: e297602fd75148f89d801f98e3ad8f9f
msgid "Install the ArduPilot Arduino in a separate folder, and add the apm/boards.txt file into the hardware folder - like the above instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:281
#: 4e4fed9749dc44c9b741f90aa73cf442
msgid "In Atmel (or Visual) Studio, in Tools>>Options>>Visual Micro, set the Applications and Arduino locations to reference the ArduPilot Arduino that supports the 2.x.x revisions, and to the folder containing the 2.x.x source code. You can get the 2.9.1b code at the `diydrones/ardupilot <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__ repository, select the desired ardupilot branch, then click download zip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-ardupilot-apm-with-visual-studio-visual-micro.rst:287
#: 16b5edee13a34d15b69209faaa597ccf
msgid "Set Tools>>Visual Micro>>Boards to APM Arduino Mega 2560."
